<title>AUSTRIA: Venezuela output at 2.48 mln bpd - Arrieta.</title>
<headline>Venezuela output at 2.48 mln bpd - Arrieta.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Venezuelan oil minister Erwin Jose Arrieta said his country was currently producing at 2.48 million barrels per day.</p>
<p>He said potential production capacity stands at 3.2 million bpd but that output fell a long way short of that figure.</p>
<p>&quot;I wish we were able to do that but that is not the case,&quot; Arietta told a news conference. &quot;Without taking into account domestic consumption the figure is in the order of 2.48 million barrels per day.&quot;</p>
<p>He estimated domestic consumption at 360,000 bpd.</p>
<p>Venezuela has an OPEC quota of 2.359 million bpd but independent observers say it produced 3.15 million bpd in October.  </p>
<p>-- Vienna Newsroom +431 713 2034</p>
</text>
